ui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\"><span style=\"font-size:20px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">I used to make strawberry fruit roll ups with my Grandma years ago so I&nbsp;thought we should try this with our cherries. It&#39;s fabulous! I cook&nbsp;pitted cherries with just a touch of water and little sugar for about 10 minutes then puree&nbsp;them in the blender. Spread the puree out on a sheet pan lined with plastic wrap and let it sun dry. Cut it into strips and enjoy!</span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-jx81lihp":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us."}},"comp-jx859xth":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us."}},"comp-jx83o6qq":{"alt":"Canned Rainier Cherries","width":4032,"height":3024,"uri":"577c92_5b57c401aeb3405089a5b2df794e5c5c~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg","name":"20190617_120437.jpg","containerId":"comp-jx83o6qq","hasBgScrollEffect":"","bgEffectName":"","displayMode":"fill","link":{},"encoding":"AVIF","allowWebpAvifTransforms":true,"responsiveImageProps":{"fallbackSrc":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_5b57c401aeb3405089a5b2df794e5c5c~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg/v1/fill/w_405,h_305,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20190617_120437.jpg","srcset":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_5b57c401aeb3405089a5b2df794e5c5c~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg/v1/fill/w_405,h_305,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20190617_120437.jpg 1x, https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_5b57c401aeb3405089a5b2df794e5c5c~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg/v1/fill/w_810,h_610,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20190617_120437.jpg 2x","css":{"container":{"position":"relative"},