extNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-jx81lis9":{"html":"<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">For Sun Dried Cherries</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"color:#1c1c1c;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Rinse the cherries and remove the stones. Cut them in half, then place them on a sheet pan cut side up in the sun. Cover them with clean screen to keep the bugs away let them dry. After bringing them in letting them cool to about 70 degrees, put them in airtight plastic containers. They will keep for a few weeks.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"color:#1c1c1c;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"color:#1c1c1c;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">For Frozen Cherries</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#1c1c1c;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Rinse the cherries and remove the pits with a cherry pitter. Toss them into reusable foil pans or onto sheet pans and freeze them in a single layer so they stay separated.&nbsp;After they are frozen you can put them into freezer bags and keep them for up to 18 months.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">For Fruit Leather&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Fresh Cherries, rinsed, pits removed</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">sugar to taste</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">3 tablespoons water to every 4 quarts of cherries</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#1c1c1c;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Cook the cherries with the water and sugar for about 10 minutes then puree&nbsp;them in the blender. Spread the puree out on a sheet pan lined with plastic wrap and let it sun dry. Cut it into strips and enjoy!</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">For the Pie Filling</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\">5-6 cups cherries cooked uncovered on the stove top for 10 minutes with 3 tablespoons water and 4 tablespoons sugar or use cherries canned in extra light syrup.</p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\">1/3-1/2 cup granulated sugar</p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\">1 tablespoon cinnamon</p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\">1 1/2 tablespoons cornstarch</p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">For the Pastry Crusts</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\">I cheated and bought frozen puff pastry sheets and refrigerator pie crusts.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-jx81lith":{"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/637329784743620019/","isConsentPolicyActive":false,"isMobile":false,"translations":{"componentName":"Share from Pinterest","large_element_one_cookie":"<%=componentname%> was blocked due to your <%=cookietype%> cookie settings. <url>Update your settings<url> ","large_element_two_cookie":"<%=componentname%> was blocked due to your <%=cookietype%> and <%=cookietype%> cookie settings. <url>Update your settings<url>","medium_element_one_cookie":"To view <%=componentname%>, <url>adjust your <%=cookietype%> cookie settings.<url>","medium_element_two_cookie":"To view <%=componentname%>, <url>adjust your <%=cookietype%> and <%=cookietype%> cookie settings.<url>","small_element_one_cookie":"<url>Update your cookie settings<url>","small_element_two_cookie":"<url>Update your cookie settings<url>","small_tooltip_one_cookie":"To view <%=componentname%>, update your <%=cookietype%> settings.","small_tooltip_two_cookie":"To view <%=componentname%>, update your <%=cookietype%> and <%=cookietype%> settings.","small_element_aria_label":"More info","tiny_element_one_cookie":"<%=componentname%> was blocked due to your <%=cookietype%> cookie settings. <url>Update your settings<url>","tiny_element_two_cookie":"<%=componentname%> was blocked due to your <%=cookietype%> and <%=cookietype%> cookie settings. <url>Update your settings<url>","tiny_element_aria_label":"Unblo